# Agent/session tooling artifacts (local-only; never versioned).
# Also keeps Codex headless review payloads under its 1 MiB input limit —
# these dirs (docs/superpowers alone is >1 MiB) were being inlined into the
# council adversarial-review prompt and tripping "Input exceeds maximum length".
.council/
.cursor/
.firecrawl/
.superpowers/
.understand-anything/
.vite/
docs/superpowers/
docs/handoffs/
# graphify-out/ is versioned here (fork/local-main only — Recipe A in
# FORK-WORKFLOW.md keeps it out of upstream PRs by branch discipline, not by
# gitignore). Overrides the machine-wide default in ~/.config/git/ignore and
# this repo's own .git/info/exclude, both of which still ignore it globally.
# Anchored to the repo root only — per-subfolder graphify-out/ dirs (e.g. from
# a multi-subfolder `graphify extract`) stay ignored as merge intermediates.
!/graphify-out/
/graphify-out/cost.json
# Regenerable scratch inside graphify-out/ — never worth versioning.
# (gitignore has no inline-comment syntax: a trailing "# ..." is part of the
# pattern, not a comment — each rule gets its own comment line above it.)
# AST extraction cache, rebuilt by any `graphify extract`:
/graphify-out/cache/
# Dated backups written by cluster-only/label before overwrite:
/graphify-out/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]/
# Machine-local interpreter path, breaks on another machine/CI:
/graphify-out/.graphify_python
# Intermediate; the full skill pipeline (Step 9) deletes it itself:
/graphify-out/.graphify_analysis.json
# Local-only: codebase-memory-mcp team graph artifact (regenerable by re-indexing)
.codebase-memory/
Music/
.npmrc

# Superpowers generated planning artifacts
/docs/superpowers/

# ...except they ARE versioned here (fork/local-main only), same deal as
# graphify-out/ above: plans and specs are this Beta's decision history and are
# worth more than a clean `git status`. Must come AFTER both rules above (l.94
# unanchored, l.121 anchored) — a negation only works once every matching rule
# has been seen. Anchored to the repo root, so a nested docs/superpowers/ inside
# a worktree stays ignored.
# What keeps this off upstream is NOT this file: it is .git/hooks/pre-push
# (fail-closed on local-only paths) plus FORK-WORKFLOW.md Recipe A. Versioning
# and shipping are separate concerns.
# NOTE: this re-inlines ~4.6 MB into any tool that reads the working tree —
# see the 1 MiB Codex-review limit noted at l.86. If /council-pr trips
# "Input exceeds maximum length" again, fix it in the council's file selection,
# not by re-ignoring this tree.
!/docs/superpowers/

